;; Frozen BLAKE3-256 (unkeyed, 32-byte output) official known-answer
;; vectors for Phase H0 of the DaoJing multihash content-addressing
;; rollout (docs/design/dao.jing.hash-registry.md). EDN, per the
;; directive's "blake3-vectors.json (or .edn)" latitude, to share one
;; portable clojure.edn reader with digest-table.edn across JVM,
;; ClojureScript, and ClojureDart test lanes.
;;
;; official-vectors uses the standard official BLAKE3 test-vector input
;; sequence input[i] = i mod 251, at the listed byte lengths: empty,
;; sub-block, single-block, chunk-boundary-adjacent (1023/1024/1025
;; straddle BLAKE3's 1024-byte chunk length), and multi-chunk (2048 = 2
;; chunks, 16384 = 16 chunks).
;;
;; non-ascii-utf8-vectors hash the UTF-8 encoding of each string;
;; :utf8-len is the encoded byte length, not the character count.
;;
;; Every hash is lowercase hex, 64 characters (32 bytes).

{:input-rule "input[i] = i % 251"

